<p>Hi Nemo,</p>

<p>This is an update regarding what we've been up to at Razorpay. This tiny newsletter
will link you to the latest changes in our API and the new features we recently released
as well as the things we are working on. Most sections link to their own blog posts,
and you can check out the links individually. Thanks for signing up with Razorpay,
and as always, you can reach out to us at contact@razorpay.com for any queries (or
just reply to this email).</p>

<h2>New Payment Status</h2>

<p>In the only minor change to the API, we are adding a new status to the Payment object,
"refunded". A payment status is set to refunded if and only if the payment
is completely refunded. For partial refunds, the status remains the same at "captured".
However, for a payment that is auto-refunded after not being captured, it is refunded
completely and its status is set to "refunded" as well.</p>

<p>This brings the total of payment status categories to 4: "created, authorized, captured
, refunded".</p>

<p>More details are at the <a href="">detailed post</a>.</p>

<h2>Wallet Updates</h2>

<p>For a while now, we have been working hard to integrate with Indian wallet systems.
A lot of our merchants are already live on PayTM, and we are happy to announce that
Mobiqwik will be available soon as a wallet option as well. The PayTM integration
is currently unavailable because of issues on PayTM's side, but it should be back
up soon.</p>

<h2>Activation Time</h2>

<p>This is where we are currently working hardest and trying to get each and every
one of you onboarded as quickly as possible. We are working to achieve instant
activations and completely online onboarding process for everyone. Meanwhile, we
are at work continuously to improve the onboarding process for every one as well
</p>

<h2>Email Updates</h2>

<p>Customers are automatically notified upon every payment being made via email.
We are also sending out Daily Transaction Reports to all merchants as well.
If you wish to disable the customer emails (for eg, if you send your own)
or if you want to change your transaction report email, let us know.
</p>

<h2>Referrals</h2>

<p>We now have a referral system for merchants in place. Reply to this mail to get
more details on it. This is especially helpful if you are an incubator, for eg.
</p>

<h2>Dashboard Updates</h2>
We have made lots of tiny changes to the merchant dashboard. You can now filter
payments by status. If you wish to see a particular feature, let us know.

<h2>Hiring &amp; Company Updates</h2>

<p>We started Razorpay with a vision to improve the state of payments in India.
Moving ahead, we have shifted operations to Bangalore, and are currently hiring
for developer roles. If you are interested (or know someone who might be), drop
us a mail at jobs@razorpay.com.
</p>

